{"id":"d5301a4f5487db1d7e8d87daf7828225b95b1774","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"d5301a4f5487db1d7e8d87daf7828225b95b1774","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/serving/expert_parallel_deployment.md","lines":["@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ vLLM provides multiple communication backends for EP. Use `--all2all-backend` to"," | `flashinfer_nvlink_one_sided` | MNNVL systems | FlashInfer's one-sided A2A strategy for multi-node NVLink | High-throughput workloads |"," | `passthrough` | Any | Internal, not accepted on the CLI: bound automatically for MoE backends that dispatch and combine themselves, so no all-to-all runs in the framework | `--moe-backend flashinfer_moe_ep_*` (FlashInfer MoE-EP megakernels) |"," | `flashinfer_nvlink_two_sided` | MNNVL systems | FlashInfer's two-sided A2A strategy for multi-node NVLink | Systems with NVLink across nodes |","+| `mori` | ROCm | MoRI EP: EPv2 (dispatch/combine over a CCO symmetric-memory window) where supported, otherwise EPv1 | AMD Instinct; see [MoRI EP](#mori-ep-rocm) |"," "," ## Single Node Deployment"," ","@@ -80,6 +81,48 @@ vllm serve deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3-0324 \\","     --enable-expert-parallel         # Enable expert parallelism"," ```"," ","+### MoRI EP (ROCm)","+","+`--all2all-backend mori` moves MoE tokens with MoRI. It runs MoRI EPv2 (`mori.ops.dispatch_combine_v2`, which reads and writes peer GPU memory directly through a MoRI CCO symmetric-memory window) where EPv2 is supported, and MoRI EPv1 otherwise.","+","+```bash","+VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MOE=1 \\","+VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FUSION_SHARED_EXPERTS=0 \\","+vllm serve deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro \\","+    --tensor-parallel-size 1 \\","+    --data-parallel-size 8 \\","+    --enable-expert-parallel \\","+    --all2all-backend mori","+```","+","+`VLLM_MORI_EP_V2` selects the MoRI version:","+","+| `VLLM_MORI_EP_V2` | Behavior |","+| ----------------- | -------- |","+| unset | EPv2, falling back to EPv1 with a warning when MoRI is older than 1.2.4, the GPU is not gfx950 or gfx1250, EP spans hosts (except on gfx1250, whose UALink team can span hosts), `MORI_ENABLE_SDMA=1`, `--moe-backend aiter_mega_moe`, the model is not BF16, or MoE activations use per-tensor FP8 |","+| `1` | Always EPv2. The checks above only log a warning; startup fails if the EP ranks are not in one CCO-LSA team |","+| `0` | EPv1 |","+","+On EPv1, `mori` uses the IntraNode kernel within one node. Across nodes it uses InterNodeV1LL when the per-rank token budget (`--max-num-batched-tokens`) is at most `VLLM_MORI_DISPATCH_INTER_KERNEL_SWITCH_THRESHOLD` (default 256), and InterNodeV1 otherwise. `mori_high_throughput` and `mori_low_latency` always run EPv1 and pin the inter-node kernel to InterNodeV1 and InterNodeV1LL respectively.","+","+Choosing a MoRI backend: use EPv2 wherever it applies, and EPv1 for deployments EPv2 does not support. EPv2 cuts its receive buffers to the rows a step can actually receive and lets AITER fused MoE write its output straight into the combine buffer, so it does less work per step than EPv1.","+","+| Deployment | Backend |","+| ---------- | ------- |","+| EP within one node (or one gfx1250 UALink fabric), BF16 model, AITER fused MoE | `mori` (runs EPv2) |","+| EP within one node, with experts that take activations quantized before dispatch (e.g. FP8 or INT8 Triton experts) | EPv2 rejects these experts at startup. Enable AITER fused MoE (`VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MOE=1`) so `mori` runs EPv2 with AITER experts; MoRI EPv1 (`VLLM_MORI_EP_V2=0`) also needs AITER fused MoE. To keep Triton experts without AITER, use a non-MoRI backend such as `allgather_reducescatter` |","+| EP across nodes | `mori` (falls back to EPv1; picks InterNodeV1LL when the per-rank token budget is at most `VLLM_MORI_DISPATCH_INTER_KERNEL_SWITCH_THRESHOLD`, else InterNodeV1) |","+","+Within one node, all EPv1 options run the same IntraNode kernel. To pin the inter-node kernel, set the threshold: `0` always picks InterNodeV1, and a value at least the per-rank token budget always picks InterNodeV1LL. `mori_high_throughput` and `mori_low_latency` do the same pinning but are deprecated and will be removed in a future release; use `mori` instead.","+","+EPv2 limitations:","+","+- All EP ranks must be in one MoRI CCO-LSA team, i.e. GPUs that can load and store each other's memory: one node, or one UALink fabric. Startup fails otherwise; there is no multi-node RDMA path yet.","+- Activations are dispatched in BF16, so the model dtype must be BF16 and the experts must take unquantized inputs (AITER fused MoE, which quantizes after the all-to-all, or BF16 experts). Experts that expect activations quantized before dispatch, such as FP8 or INT8 Triton experts, are rejected at startup. Block FP8 and MXFP4 weights work; per-tensor FP8 activations (`--quantization fp8` without blocks, ModelOpt FP8) do not, since AITER cannot quantize the received rows per tensor.","+- AITER shared-expert fusion is not supported: set `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FUSION_SHARED_EXPERTS=0`.","+- Install a MoRI build that ships `mori.ops.dispatch_combine_v2`. On NICs that limit a registered memory region to 2 GiB, the window registration fails once the dispatch arena outgrows that limit (DeepSeek-V4-Pro at EP8 already does at the default 16k batched tokens).","+- Older MoRI builds leave a stale HIP error behind when the fabric-handle probe fails (e.g. on a single MI355X node), and the next PyTorch allocation raises `operation not supported`.","+"," ## Multi-Node Deployment"," "," For multi-node deployment, use the DeepEP communication kernel with one of two modes (see [Backend Selection Guide](#backend-selection-guide) above)."],"additions":43,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/kernels/moe/modular_kernel_tools/common.py","lines":["@@ -247,6 +247,9 @@ def make_env_data(self) -> tuple[VllmConfig, dict[Any, Any]]:","             env_dict[\"VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MOE_A4W4_DSV4\"] = \"1\""," ","         vllm_config.parallel_config.all2all_backend = self.all2all_backend()","+        # \"mori\" labels the MORI EPv2 prepare/finalize here.","+        if self.all2all_backend() == \"mori\":","+            vllm_config.parallel_config.mori_ep_v2 = True"," ","         return vllm_config, env_dict"," ","@@ -366,7 +369,11 @@ def needs_aiter(self):"," ","     def needs_mori(self):","         info = prepare_finalize_info(self.prepare_finalize_type)","-        return info.backend in (\"mori_high_throughput\", \"mori_low_latency\")","+        return info.backend in (","+            \"mori_high_throughput\",","+            \"mori_low_latency\",","+            \"mori\",","+        )"," ","     def all2all_backend(self):","         info = prepare_finalize_info(self.prepare_finalize_type)"],"additions":8,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/kernels/moe/modular_kernel_tools/mk_objects.py","lines":["@@ -257,6 +257,19 @@ def expert_info(kind) -> ExpertInfo:","         supports_apply_weight_on_input=False,","     )"," ","+    from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.prepare_finalize.mori_epv2 import (","+        MoriEPv2PrepareAndFinalize,","+    )","+","+    register_prepare_and_finalize(","+        MoriEPv2PrepareAndFinalize,","+        standard_format,","+        [torch.bfloat16],","+        blocked_quantization_support=False,","+        backend=\"mori\",","+        supports_apply_weight_on_input=False,","+    )","+"," if has_flashinfer_cutlass_fused_moe() and current_platform.has_device_capability(100):","     from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts.flashinfer_cutlass_moe import (","         FlashInferExperts,"],"additions":13,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/kernels/moe/test_moe_layer.py","lines":["@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ def on_gfx950() -> bool:"," BACKENDS = [\"allgather_reducescatter\"]"," "," if has_mori():","-    BACKENDS += [\"mori_high_throughput\", \"mori_low_latency\"]","+    BACKENDS += [\"mori_high_throughput\", \"mori_low_latency\", \"mori\"]"," "," if has_flashinfer_nvlink_two_sided():","     BACKENDS += [\"flashinfer_nvlink_two_sided\"]","@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ def on_gfx950() -> bool:","     # DeepEP forces IBGDA on, so also hide the NICs from it.","     \"NVSHMEM_HCA_LIST\": \"none\","," }","-MORI_BACKENDS = {\"mori_high_throughput\", \"mori_low_latency\"}","+MORI_BACKENDS = {\"mori_high_throughput\", \"mori_low_latency\", \"mori\"}"," "," QUANT_METHODS = [","     None,","@@ -151,6 +151,8 @@ def on_gfx950() -> bool:","     \"allgather_reducescatter\":     {None,         \"fp8\", \"modelopt_fp8\", \"modelopt_fp4\"}, # noqa: E501","     \"mori_high_throughput\":        {None,         \"fp8\", \"modelopt_fp8\"},","     \"mori_low_latency\":            {None,         \"fp8\", \"modelopt_fp8\"},","+    # Pinned to EPv2, which rejects per-tensor FP8 activations.","+    \"mori\":                        {None, \"fp8_blocked\"},","     \"flashinfer_nvlink_two_sided\": {None, \"fp8_blocked\",                 \"modelopt_fp4\"}, # noqa: E501","     \"flashinfer_nvlink_one_sided\": {None, \"fp8_blocked\",                 \"modelopt_fp4\"}, # noqa: E501","     \"deepep_low_latency\":          {None, \"fp8_blocked\",                 \"modelopt_fp4\"}, # noqa: E501","@@ -163,6 +165,7 @@ def on_gfx950() -> bool:","     \"allgather_reducescatter\":     (True,  True,  True,  True),","     \"mori_high_throughput\":        (True, False, False,  True),","     \"mori_low_latency\":            (True, False, False,  True),","+    \"mori\":                        (True, False, False,  True),","     \"flashinfer_nvlink_two_sided\": (False, True, False, False),","     \"flashinfer_nvlink_one_sided\": (True,  True, False, False),","     \"deepep_low_latency\":          (True, False, False,  True),","@@ -2189,6 +2192,8 @@ def test_moe_layer(","         tensor_parallel_size=tp_size,","         enable_expert_parallel=use_ep,","         all2all_backend=backend,","+        # Pin \"mori\" to EPv2; mori_high_throughput/mori_low_latency cover EPv1.","+        mori_ep_v2=True if backend == \"mori\" else None,","         enable_eplb=enable_eplb,","         eplb_config=eplb_config,","     )"],"additions":7,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/kernels/moe/test_mori_epv2_prepare_finalize.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,471 @@","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+\"\"\"MORI EPv2 prepare/finalize and all2all manager, with MORI faked out.\"\"\"","+","+import sys","+from datetime import timedelta","+from types import SimpleNamespace","+from unittest.mock import Mock","+","+import pytest","+import torch","+import torch.distributed as dist","+import torch.multiprocessing as mp","+","+import vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.prepare_finalize.mori_epv2 as mori_epv2","+import vllm.utils.import_utils as import_utils","+from vllm.config.parallel import resolve_mori_all2all","+from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.prepare_finalize.mori_epv2 import (","+    MoriEPv2PrepareAndFinalize,","+)","+from vllm.utils.network_utils import get_open_port","+","+","+class FakeOp:","+    \"\"\"MORI EPv2 op whose receive buffers have `capacity` rows, `recv` valid.\"\"\"","+","+    def __init__(self, capacity=256, recv=0):","+        self.routing = object()","+        self.recv_a1 = torch.full((capacity, 4), float(\"nan\"), dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+        self.recv_weights = torch.full((capacity, 2), float(\"inf\"))","+        self.recv_ids = torch.full((capacity, 2), 5, dtype=torch.int32)","+        self.recv = recv","+        self.combine_in = torch.empty(capacity, 4, dtype=torch.bfloat16)","+        self.sent_ids: torch.Tensor | None = None","+        self.combine_input: torch.Tensor | None = None","+        self.combine_routing = None","+","+    def combine_in_view(self):","+        return self.combine_in","+","+    def dispatch(self, input, weights, scales, indices, *, return_routing=True):","+        self.sent_ids = indices","+        return (","+            self.recv_a1,","+            self.recv_weights,","+            None,","+            self.recv_ids,","+            torch.tensor([self.recv], dtype=torch.int32),","+            self.routing,","+        )","+","+    def combine(self, input, weights=None, indices=None, *, routing):","+        self.combine_input = input","+        self.combine_routing = routing","+        return torch.zeros(1, 4, dtype=torch.bfloat16), None","+","+","+def _make_pf(op, num_local_experts=2, rank_expert_offset=0):","+    return MoriEPv2PrepareAndFinalize(op, 16, 4, num_local_experts, rank_expert_offset)","+","+","+def _run(monkeypatch, op, num_tokens_across_dp, topk_ids, **pf_kwargs):","+    \"\"\"One prepare + finalize round trip under the given DP token counts.\"\"\"","+    if num_tokens_across_dp is None:","+        ctx = SimpleNamespace(dp_metadata=None)","+    else:","+        counts = torch.tensor(num_tokens_across_dp)","+        ctx = SimpleNamespace(","+            dp_metadata=SimpleNamespace(num_tokens_across_dp_cpu=counts)","+        )","+    monkeypatch.setattr(mori_epv2, \"is_forward_context_available\", lambda: True)","+    monkeypatch.setattr(mori_epv2, \"get_forward_context\", lambda: ctx)","+    monkeypatch.setattr(","+        mori_epv2, \"get_dp_group\", lambda: SimpleNamespace(rank_in_group=0)","+    )","+    monkeypatch.setattr(torch.cuda, \"is_current_stream_capturing\", lambda: False)","+    prepare_finalize = _make_pf(op, **pf_kwargs)","+    num_tokens = topk_ids.shape[0]","+    prepared = prepare_finalize.prepare(","+        torch.ones(num_tokens, 4, dtype=torch.bfloat16),","+        torch.ones(num_tokens, 2, dtype=torch.bfloat16),","+        topk_ids,","+        num_experts=8,","+        expert_map=None,","+        apply_router_weight_on_input=False,","+        quant_config=SimpleNamespace(is_per_tensor=False, a1_scale=None),","+    )","+    prepare_finalize.finalize(","+        torch.empty(num_tokens, 4, dtype=torch.bfloat16),","+        prepared[0],","+        prepared[4],","+        prepared[3],","+        False,","+        SimpleNamespace(),","+    )","+    return prepared","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    \"num_tokens_across_dp,recv,rows\",","+    [","+        # Sum of DP batches (6) rounded up to 32 rows, of 256 capacity rows.","+        ([1, 3, 2, 0], 7, 32),","+        ([33, 0, 0, 0], 20, 64),","+        # TP=2 per DP rank: each TP rank may send its DP batch, 2 * 50 rows.","+        ([30, 20], 90, 128),","+        # Dispatchers not a multiple of DP ranks: dispatchers * largest batch.","+        ([10, 20, 5], 60, 96),","+        # Bound above capacity: keep the full buffer.","+        ([100, 100, 100, 100], 200, 256),","+        # No DP metadata, or stale metadata missing this rank's batch: full buffer.","+        (None, 7, 256),","+        ([0, 3, 2, 0], 5, 256),","+    ],","+)","+def test_receive_rows_are_bounded_by_dp_tokens(","+    monkeypatch, num_tokens_across_dp, recv, rows","+):","+    op = FakeOp(recv=recv)","+    a1, _, meta, ids, weights = _run(","+        monkeypatch, op, num_tokens_across_dp, torch.tensor([[0, 1]])","+    )","+    for t, buf in ((a1, op.recv_a1), (ids, op.recv_ids), (weights, op.recv_weights)):","+        assert t.shape[0] == rows","+        assert t.data_ptr() == buf.data_ptr()  # views, no copy","+    # Rows past the receive count are cleared; rows past the bound are untouched.","+    assert torch.isnan(a1[:recv]).all() and (a1[recv:] == 0).all()","+    assert (ids[:recv] == 5).all() and (ids[recv:] == -1).all()","+    assert (weights[recv:] == 0).all()","+    assert torch.isnan(op.recv_a1[rows:]).all()","+    assert int(meta.expert_num_tokens) == recv","+    # combine sees only the bounded expert output, under dispatch's routing.","+    assert op.combine_input is not None and op.combine_input.shape[0] == rows","+    assert op.combine_routing is op.routing","+","+","+def test_padding_tokens_are_routed_to_local_experts(monkeypatch):","+    op = FakeOp(recv=2)","+    # Rank 1 of 4 with 2 experts each owns experts 2 and 3. The second token is","+    # DP padding, which the router marks with expert id -1.","+    topk_ids = torch.tensor([[0, 7], [-1, -1]])","+    _run(monkeypatch, op, None, topk_ids, num_local_experts=2, rank_expert_offset=2)","+    assert op.sent_ids is not None and op.sent_ids.dtype == torch.int32","+    assert op.sent_ids.tolist() == [[0, 7], [2, 3]]","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"world_size,lsa_size\", [(8, 8), (8, 4)])","+def test_manager_requires_one_lsa_team(monkeypatch, world_size, lsa_size):","+    from vllm.distributed.device_communicators import all2all","+    from vllm.distributed.device_communicators.base_device_communicator import (","+        All2AllManagerBase,","+    )","+","+    monkeypatch.setattr(","+        All2AllManagerBase,","+        \"__init__\",","+        lambda self, group: self.__dict__.update(","+            rank=0, world_size=world_size, cpu_group=group","+        ),","+    )","+    monkeypatch.setattr(","+        torch.distributed, \"broadcast_object_list\", lambda *a, **k: None","+    )","+    monkeypatch.setattr(all2all, \"CudaRTLibrary\", Mock)","+    device_comm = Mock(lsa_size=lsa_size)","+    calls = Mock()  # records the order of op.close and comm.destroy","+    comm = calls.comm","+    comm.create_dev_comm.return_value = device_comm","+    communicator = Mock()","+    communicator.init.return_value = comm","+    monkeypatch.setitem(","+        sys.modules,","+        \"mori.cco\",","+        SimpleNamespace(","+            Communicator=communicator,","+            CCODevCommRequirements=SimpleNamespace,","+            GDA_CONNECTION_NONE=0,","+        ),","+    )","+    if lsa_size != world_size:","+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"one LSA team\"):","+            all2all.MoriEPv2All2AllManager(object())","+    else:","+        cfg = dict(","+            scale_dim=0,","+            scale_type_size=4,","+            num_experts_per_token=8,","+            token_nbytes=4096,","+            combine_token_nbytes=4096,","+            effective_max_recv=1024,","+            dispatch_dtype=None,","+            combine_dtype=None,","+            schedule=None,","+        )","+        monkeypatch.setitem(","+            sys.modules,","+            \"mori.ops.dispatch_combine_v2\",","+            SimpleNamespace(","+                EpDispatchCombineConfig=lambda **kw: SimpleNamespace(**(cfg | kw)),","+                EpDispatchCombineOp=lambda config, comm: calls.op,","+            ),","+        )","+        manager = all2all.MoriEPv2All2AllManager(object())","+        assert manager.get_handle({}) is calls.op","+        # The cache holds ops weakly; the manager keeps them alive itself.","+        manager.handle_cache._cache.clear()","+        manager.destroy()","+        # Ops live in the communicator's window: they must go first.","+        order = [c[0] for c in calls.mock_calls]","+        assert order.index(\"op.close\") < order.index(\"comm.destroy\")","+    device_comm.close.assert_called_once()","+    comm.destroy.assert_called_once()","+","+","+def _unique_id_worker(rank, init_method):","+    from vllm.distributed.device_communicators import all2all","+    from vllm.distributed.device_communicators.base_device_communicator import (","+        All2AllManagerBase,","+    )","+","+    dist.init_process_group(","+        \"gloo\",","+        init_method=init_method,","+        rank=rank,","+        world_size=4,","+        timeout=timedelta(seconds=60),","+    )","+    # With PP=2 and DP=2 the EP groups are [0, 2] and [1, 3].","+    groups = [dist.new_group([0, 2]), dist.new_group([1, 3])]","+    group = groups[rank % 2]","+","+    def fake_init(self, g):","+        self.__dict__.update(rank=g.rank(), world_size=g.size(), cpu_group=g)","+","+    All2AllManagerBase.__init__ = fake_init  # type: ignore[method-assign]","+    all2all.CudaRTLibrary = Mock  # type: ignore[misc]","+    communicator = Mock()","+    communicator.get_unique_id.return_value = f\"uid-of-rank-{rank}\"","+    communicator.init.return_value.create_dev_comm.return_value = Mock(lsa_size=2)","+    sys.modules[\"mori.cco\"] = SimpleNamespace(","+        Communicator=communicator,","+        CCODevCommRequirements=SimpleNamespace,","+        GDA_CONNECTION_NONE=0,","+    )","+    all2all.MoriEPv2All2AllManager(group)","+    # Every rank joins the communicator with the ID its group's first rank made.","+    assert communicator.init.call_args.args[2] == f\"uid-of-rank-{rank % 2}\"","+    dist.destroy_process_group()","+","+","+def test_unique_id_comes_from_the_ep_groups_first_rank():","+    mp.spawn(_unique_id_worker, args=(f\"tcp://127.0.0.1:{get_open_port()}\",), nprocs=4)","+","+","+def test_experts_write_into_combine_staging_only_when_it_fits():","+    from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.topk_weight_and_reduce import (","+        TopKWeightAndReduceContiguous,","+        TopKWeightAndReduceNoOP,","+    )","+","+    op = FakeOp()","+    alloc = _make_pf(op).allocate_fused_expert_output","+    device = op.combine_in.device","+    out = alloc((32, 4), torch.bfloat16, device, TopKWeightAndReduceNoOP())","+    assert out is not None and out.shape == (32, 4)","+    assert out.data_ptr() == op.combine_in.data_ptr()","+    # Unreduced expert output, other dtypes or too many rows keep the workspace.","+    for args in (","+        ((32, 4), torch.bfloat16, device, TopKWeightAndReduceContiguous()),","+        ((32, 4), torch.float32, device, TopKWeightAndReduceNoOP()),","+        ((257, 4), torch.bfloat16, device, TopKWeightAndReduceNoOP()),","+    ):","+        assert alloc(*args) is None","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    \"in_dtype,quant_dtype,quantizes_itself,per_tensor,ok\",","+    [","+        (torch.bfloat16, None, False, False, True),","+        # e.g. AITER, which quantizes after the all2all.","+        (torch.bfloat16, torch.float8_e4m3fn, True, False, True),","+        # AITER cannot quantize the received rows per tensor.","+        (torch.bfloat16, torch.float8_e4m3fn, True, True, False),","+        # e.g. FP8 Triton experts, which expect the dispatch to quantize.","+        (torch.bfloat16, torch.float8_e4m3fn, False, False, False),","+        (torch.float16, None, False, False, False),","+    ],","+)","+def test_experts_it_cannot_feed_are_rejected(","+    in_dtype, quant_dtype, quantizes_itself, per_tensor, ok","+):","+    experts = SimpleNamespace(","+        moe_config=SimpleNamespace(in_dtype=in_dtype),","+        quant_config=SimpleNamespace(quant_dtype=quant_dtype, is_per_tensor=per_tensor),","+        expects_unquantized_inputs=quantizes_itself,","+    )","+    prepare_finalize = _make_pf(FakeOp(16))","+    if ok:","+        prepare_finalize.post_init_setup(experts)","+    else:","+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"VLLM_MORI_EP_V2=0\"):","+            prepare_finalize.post_init_setup(experts)","+","+","+def _parallel_config(**overrides):","+    fields = dict(","+        all2all_backend=\"mori\",","+        mori_ep_v2=None,","+        tensor_parallel_size=1,","+        data_parallel_size=8,","+        data_parallel_size_local=8,","+        data_parallel_external_lb=False,","+        data_parallel_backend=\"mp\",","+        nnodes_within_dp=1,","+        prefill_context_parallel_size=1,","+    )","+    return SimpleNamespace(**(fields | overrides))","+","+","+def _model_config(quant_cfg=None, **overrides):","+    fields = {\"dtype\": torch.bfloat16, \"quantization\": None}","+    arch = SimpleNamespace(quantization_config=quant_cfg)","+    return SimpleNamespace(model_arch_config=arch, **(fields | overrides))","+","+","+_EXTERNAL_LB = {\"data_parallel_size_local\": 1, \"data_parallel_external_lb\": True}","+_FP8_BLOCK = {\"quantization\": \"fp8\", \"quant_cfg\": {\"weight_block_size\": [128, 128]}}","+_MODELOPT_FP8 = {\"quantization\": \"modelopt\", \"quant_cfg\": {\"quant_algo\": \"FP8\"}}","+_MODELOPT_NVFP4 = {\"quantization\": \"modelopt\", \"quant_cfg\": {\"quant_algo\": \"NVFP4\"}}","+","+","+def _ct(strategy):","+    act = {\"type\": \"float\", \"num_bits\": 8, \"strategy\": strategy}","+    cfg = {\"config_groups\": {\"group_0\": {\"input_activations\": act}}}","+    return {\"quantization\": \"compressed-tensors\", \"quant_cfg\": cfg}","+","+","+def _quark(qscheme):","+    inputs = {\"dtype\": \"fp8_e4m3\", \"qscheme\": qscheme}","+    cfg = {\"global_quant_config\": {\"input_tensors\": inputs}}","+    return {\"quantization\": \"quark\", \"quant_cfg\": cfg}","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    \"parallel,model,moe_backend,env,ep_v2\",","+    [","+        ({}, {}, \"aiter\", {}, True),","+        # EP across hosts: DP over two nodes, even with ep_size <= 8.","+        ({\"data_parallel_size\": 16}, {}, \"aiter\", {}, False),","+        ({\"data_parallel_size_local\": 4}, {}, \"aiter\", {}, False),","+        # A DP replica (TP/PP) spanning nodes.","+        ({\"nnodes_within_dp\": 2}, {}, \"aiter\", {}, False),","+        # External LB only sees its own rank: fall back to the EP size.","+        (_EXTERNAL_LB, {}, \"aiter\", {}, True),","+        (_EXTERNAL_LB | {\"data_parallel_size\": 16}, {}, \"aiter\", {}, False),","+        # The LSA team may span hosts (gfx1250); the manager checks it.","+        ({\"data_parallel_size\": 16, \"lsa_spans_hosts\": True}, {}, \"aiter\", {}, True),","+        ({}, {}, \"aiter\", {\"MORI_ENABLE_SDMA\": \"1\"}, False),","+        # gfx1250 keeps EPv2 under SDMA.","+        ({\"sdma_picks_epv1\": False}, {}, \"aiter\", {\"MORI_ENABLE_SDMA\": \"1\"}, True),","+        ({}, {}, \"aiter_mega_moe\", {}, False),","+        ({}, {\"dtype\": torch.float16}, \"aiter\", {}, False),","+        # An explicit VLLM_MORI_EP_V2 wins over the deployment checks.","+        ({}, {\"dtype\": torch.float16}, \"aiter\", {\"VLLM_MORI_EP_V2\": \"1\"}, True),","+        ({}, {}, \"aiter\", {\"VLLM_MORI_EP_V2\": \"0\"}, False),","+        # Already resolved: kept as is.","+        ({\"mori_e